          "description": "Small, elongated body, almost perfectly cylindrical, column 15.1 mm in height and 6 mm in diameter at mid-column, divisible into scapus and short scapulus (Fig. 4 B). Tentacles without mesogleal thickenings at base, arranged in five cycles, 72 in total. Mesenteries hexamerously arranged in four cycles. Acontia present, but rare. CNIDOM. Spirocysts, basitrichs, microbasic p - mastigophores B 1 (Fig. 4 I: p – s, Table 6).",
